  "rule": "Every door must have a clear width of at least 900 mm.\n\nRegulatory text (the authoritative clauses - use them to interpret the requirement and its applicability; you must still work out how to read or measure it from the IFC):\nDIN 18040-1:2010-10 (Accessible buildings - publicly accessible buildings), 4.3.3.2 Dimensional requirements, Table 1 (paraphrased): all doors must provide a clear width of at least 90 cm.\nBenchmark convention: the clear width of a door is its overall width (IfcDoor.OverallWidth) minus twice the lining thickness recorded in the IfcDoorLiningProperties of its door type. When the door type records no lining thickness, the clear width is the overall width. A door without a recorded overall width cannot be judged: label it ALERT, and do NOT report it as a violation.\n\nLabel every door.\nReport the GlobalId of every element (modelled as IfcDoor) that does NOT satisfy this requirement.",
